### IdentityService - przykładowe żądania (Rider: HTTP Client)
@baseUrl = https://localhost:7001

### Rejestracja (link aktywacyjny trafia do Mailpit: http://localhost:8025)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "nowy@shop.local",
  "password": "Haslo1234",
  "firstName": "Anna",
  "lastName": "Nowak",
  "acceptTerms": true,
  "marketingConsent": false
}

### Potwierdzenie e-maila (userId i code z linku w e-mailu)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/confirm-email
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "userId": "00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000",
  "code": "..."
}

### Logowanie (konto z seeda)
# @name login
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "user@shop.local",
  "password": "User1234!"
}

> {%
    if (response.body.tokens) {
        client.global.set("accessToken", response.body.tokens.accessToken);
        client.global.set("refreshToken", response.body.tokens.refreshToken);
    }
    if (response.body.twoFactorToken) {
        client.global.set("twoFactorToken", response.body.twoFactorToken);
    }
%}

### Logowanie - drugi krok (kod z aplikacji Authenticator)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login/2fa
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "twoFactorToken": "{{twoFactorToken}}",
  "code": "123456"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("accessToken", response.body.tokens.accessToken);
    client.global.set("refreshToken", response.body.tokens.refreshToken);
%}

### Odświeżenie tokenu
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/refresh
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("accessToken", response.body.accessToken);
    client.global.set("refreshToken", response.body.refreshToken);
%}

### Profil
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/account/me
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Zmiana hasła
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/account/change-password
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "currentPassword": "User1234!",
  "newPassword": "NoweHaslo123"
}

### Zmiana e-maila (link potwierdzający idzie na nowy adres)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/account/change-email
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "newEmail": "jan.nowy@shop.local",
  "password": "User1234!"
}

### 2FA - status
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/account/2fa
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 2FA - wygeneruj klucz i kod QR
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/account/2fa/authenticator
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### 2FA - włącz (kod z aplikacji), zwraca kody odzyskiwania
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/account/2fa/enable
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "code": "123456"
}

### 2FA - wyłącz
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/account/2fa/disable
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "password": "User1234!"
}

### Sesje (urządzenia)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/account/sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Wyloguj wszystkie inne urządzenia
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/account/sessions
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Historia zdarzeń bezpieczeństwa
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/account/security-events?page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### RODO - zgody
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/account/privacy/consents
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### RODO - zgoda marketingowa
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/account/privacy/consents/marketing
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "granted": true
}

### RODO - eksport danych
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/account/privacy/export
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

### Admin - logowanie (konto z seeda)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@shop.local",
  "password": "Admin123!"
}

> {%
    client.global.set("adminToken", response.body.tokens.accessToken);
%}

### Admin - wyszukiwanie użytkowników
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/admin/users?search=shop.local&page=1&pageSize=20
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### Wylogowanie
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/logout
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refreshToken": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

### Klucze publiczne (dla Shop API)
GET {{baseUrl}}/.well-known/jwks.json
